  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(f(x)=\\log\\left(\\dfrac{1+x}{1-x}\\right)\\) for \\(-1\\lt x\\lt1,\\) then \\(f\\left(\\dfrac{3x+x^3}{1+3x^2}\\right)\\) in terms of \\(f(x)\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-f(x)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2f(x)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(3f(x)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\([f(x)]^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\([f(x)]^3-f(x)\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1972-p29.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(u=\\frac{3x+x^3}{1+3x^2}.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac{1+u}{1-u} &=\\frac{1+3x^2+3x+x^3} {1+3x^2-3x-x^3}\\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}\\right)^3. \\end{aligned} \\] Consequently \\[ f(u)=3\\log\\left(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}\\right)=3f(x). \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute the rational expression into \\(\\frac{1+u}{1-u}\\)",
        "Its numerator and denominator factor as \\((1+x)^3\\) and \\((1-x)^3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
